-- The interface between the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 and an Act that creates offences outside the Penal Code 1871.
--
-- THIS FILE IS DECLARE-ONLY AND IS BYTE-IDENTICAL IN THREE SUBJECTS:
--   sg/criminal-procedure-code-2010/encodings/written-law-interface.l4
--   sg/prevention-of-corruption-act-1960/encodings/written-law-interface.l4
--   sg/misuse-of-drugs-act-1973/encodings/written-law-interface.l4
-- It exists for the reason ea-cpc-interface.l4 does: `l4` resolves an IMPORT only to a module in the importing file's own directory (or
-- the project root, or the embedded library), so a subject cannot import another subject's module.  The Acts do not copy each other's
-- rules; they meet at the few answers one Act hands the Code, declared here once and copied.  Each row's check.sh checks the copies are
-- identical.  The First Schedule's last four rows and section 2(1) say that an offence under another written law is read off that law's
-- own provisions ("unless specifically empowered ... by the law offended against"; "or under any other written law"; "shown to be
-- triable ... under that law"), and this record is where that law says so.
--
-- Direction: the OFFENCE-CREATING ACT computes the record (from its own sections); the CODE row consumes it (cpc-other-laws.l4).
-- The Code's rules are not restated in the Act, and the Act's rules are not restated in the Code.

§ `What an Act tells the Code about its own offences`

@ref "Criminal Procedure Code 2010, s 2(1) 'arrestable offence', 'bailable offence'; s 9(2)(b), 9(3)(b); First Schedule, 'Offences against laws other than the Penal Code 1871'; Second Schedule"
DECLARE `Written Law Procedure Statement` HAS
    `the Act` IS A STRING
    `the Act deems the offence to be an arrestable offence for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Act empowers the police to arrest without warrant for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a District Court under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Act shows the offence as triable by a Magistrate's Court under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
